Method 2. We find that
32 − 15% of 32 = 32 − \frac{15}{100} × \frac{32}{1}
= 32 − \frac{24}{5}
= 27\frac{1}{5}
The new amount is 27.2.

It is more useful to compare the price per kilogram.
Can 1. \frac{\$3.75}{0.3\text{ kg}} = \$12.50/\text{kg}
Can 2. \frac{\$5.20}{0.4\text{ kg}} = \$13.00/\text{kg}
Can 1 offers the best value for money as the price per kilogram is lower.
